---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { docs, site } from "../config";
import { notes } from "../lib/news";
import { libraryTracks, licencePresentation } from "../data/credits";
import { loadTracks, pageUrl } from "../lib/tracks";

const tracks = loadTracks();
const pageTitle = site.title;
const pageDescription = site.seoDescription;
---

<Base title={pageTitle} description={pageDescription}>
  <div class="shell">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <p class="kicker">Station · 24/7</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">{site.name}<span class="caret" aria-hidden="true"></span></h1>
      <p class="tagline">Lo-fi for the long session, and a short bulletin when the tools change.</p>
      <p class="deck">
        People choose the music. Short English bulletins cover AI and software.
        The voices are generated, and the station says so on air.
      </p>
      <div class="actions">
        <button
          type="button"
          class="button"
          data-play
          data-label-play="Listen live"
          data-label-stop="Stop"
          aria-pressed="false"
        >
          <span data-play-label>Listen live</span>
        </button>
        <a class="button ghost" href="#submit">Submit a track</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="news" aria-labelledby="news-title">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">01</p>
        <h2 id="news-title">News</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">
          Between tracks, DevRadio reads a short English bulletin: one story about AI or software,
          written to be heard once. Some editions are a dialogue between two hosts. Both voices are
          synthetic, and that is said before the item.
        </p>
        <div class="notes">
          {
            notes.map((note) => (
              <article class="note">
                <p class="idx">{note.kicker}</p>
                <div>
                  <h3>{note.title}</h3>
                  <p>{note.body}</p>
                </div>
              </article>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <p class="fine">These notes describe the format. They are not a published archive.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="submit" aria-labelledby="submit-title">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">02</p>
        <h2 id="submit-title">Submit</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">
          The library grows by pull request. Audio files are not committed. You host the file at a
          public HTTPS URL, add <span class="mono">tracks/&lt;slug&gt;/track.yaml</span>, and CI
          downloads that URL to check the checksum. GitHub never talks to the playout server.
        </p>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>
            <span>1</span>
            <p>Fork the repository and branch from main. Use a lower-case slug of letters, digits, and hyphens.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>2</span>
            <p>Copy <span class="mono">examples/track.yaml</span> to <span class="mono">tracks/&lt;slug&gt;/track.yaml</span>. The folder name is the track id.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>3</span>
            <p>Publish the audio yourself. Set <span class="mono">audio.audio_url</span> and the SHA-256 of that exact file.</p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span>4</span>
            <p>Open the pull request and complete every attestation. A person reviews the licence before merge.</p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="doc-links">
          <a href={docs.contributing}>Contribution guide</a>
          <a href={docs.licenses}>Accepted licences</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="tracks" aria-labelledby="tracks-title">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">03</p>
        <h2 id="tracks-title">Tracks</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">
          The on-air library is {libraryTracks.length} tracks, credited on the music credits page:
          artist, Free Music Archive track page, and Creative Commons licence. Community submissions
          are listed here after they merge.
        </p>
        <p class="doc-links">
          <a href="/credits">Music credits</a>
          <a href={docs.takedown}>Takedown</a>
        </p>
        {
          tracks.length === 0 ? (
            <p class="fine">No community submissions in the index yet.</p>
          ) : (
            <ol class="credits">
              {tracks.map((track) => {
                const source = pageUrl(track.source_url);
                const licence = licencePresentation(track.licence);
                return (
                  <li class="credit">
                    <p class="idx">{track.id}</p>
                    <div>
                      <p class="credit-title">{track.title || track.id}</p>
                      {track.artist ? <p>{track.artist}</p> : null}
                      <p class="credit-meta">
                        {licence?.url ? (
                          <a href={licence.url} rel="license">{licence.name}</a>
                        ) : licence ? (
                          <span>{licence.name}</span>
                        ) : null}
                        {source ? <a href={source}>Source</a> : null}
                      </p>
                    </div>
                  </li>
                );
              })}
            </ol>
          )
        }
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="doctrine" aria-labelledby="doctrine-title">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">04</p>
        <h2 id="doctrine-title">Doctrine</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="lede">Five rules for what goes on the air.</p>
        <div class="rules">
          <article class="rule">
            <p class="idx">01</p>
            <div>
              <h3>Human-curated</h3>
              <p>A person accepts every track. Nothing lands on the station because a script found a file.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="rule">
            <p class="idx">02</p>
            <div>
              <h3>Licensed music only</h3>
              <p>
                The accepted values are CC-BY-4.0, CC-BY-SA-4.0, CC0-1.0, and SUNO-PAID-OWN, on the
                terms in the <a href={docs.licenses}>licence notes</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="rule">
            <p class="idx">03</p>
            <div>
              <h3>AI voices are disclosed</h3>
              <p>Bulletins and two-host dialogues use synthetic speech, and the broadcast says so.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="rule">
            <p class="idx">04</p>
            <div>
              <h3>Sources stay attached</h3>
              <p>Artist, licence, and source URL remain with the track, on the station and in this list.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="rule">
            <p class="idx">05</p>
            <div>
              <h3>Takedown has a path</h3>
              <p>
                A verified complaint comes off the stream and out of the repository. The procedure is
                the <a href={docs.takedown}>takedown note</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
